# Tailored resumes

The resume in `Base/` is the only source of facts. Read it before writing. A tailored resume selects, reorders, and rephrases that file for one job. It keeps the base resume's sections, heading names, contact block, and voice.

If `Base/` has no resume, stop and ask for one.

## Change only emphasis

- Lead with skills and bullets that match this job.
- Drop bullets that do not help this application when the same work is already covered.
- Use the job's terms only when the base resume already supports that work.

## Leave facts alone

Do not add or alter employers, titles, dates, education, locations, metrics, scope, or tools. If a requirement is not in the base resume, omit it.

```markdown
<!-- Base: "Built event-driven billing services on Kafka." -->
<!-- Job asks for distributed systems. -->

<!-- Good -->
- Built event-driven billing services on Kafka, processing payment events across services.

<!-- Bad: the scale is not in the base resume -->
- Designed a distributed system handling 10M events per day.
```
